    delphi:hasConfidence "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The inherited acquired-effect mechanism has a clear experimental test, and some relevant data are public. Existing comparative skeleton data alone cannot identify use and disuse as the cause." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Test whether parental use or disuse predicts offspring skeletal traits after controlling offspring activity, genotype and maternal environment, ideally across pedigrees or reciprocal interventions. Inheritance of the acquired shift supports the claim; disappearance under controls refutes it." ;
